+# FINDINGS
+
+Conclusion: I would not ship this vault to mainnet on Monday.
+
+I did not change anything under `src/`. I did not change `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` or anything under `test/mocks/`. The repros I added are:
+
+- `test/RealMainnetUsdtCompatibility.t.sol`
+- `test/WithdrawalFeeAndYieldAccounting.t.sol`
+
+## Finding 1: real mainnet USDT deposits revert before reaching Aave
+
+Severity: Critical.
+
+The vault calls:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+through the standard `IERC20` interface. Mainnet USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7` does not return a boolean from `approve`. In Solidity 0.8, a high-level call through an interface that expects a `bool` reverts while decoding the empty return data.
+
+The mainnet-fork repro funds a user with real forked USDT, approves the vault using `SafeERC20.forceApprove`, then calls `deposit` against the real USDT, real Aave V3 Pool, and real aUSDT addresses from the README. The user-side USDT transfer and approval both succeed. The vault's own raw `approve` emits `Approval`, returns no data, and then `deposit` reverts before `aavePool.supply`.
+
+Command:
+
+```bash
+forge test --match-contract RealMainnetUsdtCompatibilityTest --fork-url https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -vvvv
+```
+
